		<Section id="decisions" eyebrow="PoliVerse · The rules" title="Six rules," dim="each with its reason." index={7} link={{ label: 'Why it never writes', href: `${repo}/blob/main/docs/writes-to-university-systems.md` }}>
			<Principles rules={[
				{ title: 'Read, never write.', text: 'No enrolling, no refusing a mark, no forum posts, no hand-ins. The write requests are unverified, and a wrong one costs the student a session.', source: 'docs/writes-to-university-systems.md' },
				{ title: 'Never pass sample data off as real.', text: 'Sample data is on by default and every screen says so; all of it comes from one fictional degree, so career, timetable and courses agree.', source: 'SampleDegree · DataStatusLine' },
				{ title: 'Keep what is on screen.', text: 'A failed refresh leaves the cached copy in place and says how old it is.', source: 'Store · FreshnessBar' },
				{ title: 'Nothing leaves the phone on its own.', text: 'No analytics service and no crash reporter. Diagnostics and MetricKit reports stay on the device until the student shares them.', source: 'Diagnostics · docs/field-performance.md' },
				{ title: 'Borrow nothing that isn’t ours.', text: 'No SF Symbols in the icon, as Apple’s terms require, and nothing from the Politecnico’s identity: the app is unofficial and must not look otherwise.', source: 'design/app-icon/README.md' },
				{ title: 'Check every colour.', text: 'The brand navy is 13:1 on white but 1.3:1 on the dark background, so every accent has a dark twin. The worst pair is now 4.7:1.', source: 'Theme.swift' },
			]} />
		</Section>

